Evening: 2,799 of 2,804 flights warned; recall 100%, but false-positive rate 99.7%. ORD false-positive rate 75.5%, versus ATL 64.7%. High recall alone hides the alert burden.

Blank bars mean insufficient reporting support: group n≥200 and ≥30 relevant outcomes/warnings. AS, B6, WN and overnight have withheld rates. These cutoffs do not establish statistical certainty.
The airport control filters only the flight-detail list. Aggregate error-rate charts always show their full July groups. Hover / View Data for TP, FP, FN, TN.</run>
          </formatted-text>
